{"description":"Align eka-steward's human CLI output with the eka-cli design system so `eka steward ...` looks like `eka`. Added internal/ui (a stdlib-only deliberate mirror of eka-cli's cmd/ui: two-space left margin, ANSI 256-color palette, Unicode icon set, aligned header/table/summary renderers). `run` now prints a themed human report by default and `run --json` emits the deterministic machine report on the raw writer, byte-identical to the prior output (obs.Report.Write). `version` renders through the same style (plain, margin-indented). Colors only on a TTY with NO_COLOR unset and TERM != dumb; non-TTY stays plain text + UTF-8 icons, no ANSI. TTY detection is the stdlib char-device check (no golang.org/x/term). Refreshed the stale root help/doc. Docs: README and RELEASE_NOTES updated to the shipped surface; release.md/release-checklist.md/upgrade.md/drivers.md/build.yaml comment refreshed; cmd/readme_version_test.go pins the README version axes and scripts/bump.sh syncs the steward axis on bump. Shipped as eka-steward v2.2.0.","acceptanceCriteria":"gofmt -l empty, go vet clean, GOOS=windows build ok, go test -race -count=1 ./... all packages ok. PR #4 merged to develop. Tag v2.2.0 released with all assets (eka-steward-{linux,darwin,windows}-{amd64,arm64}[.exe], install.sh, install.ps1, SHA256SUMS.txt). Released binary prints 'eka-steward 2.2.0' and 'eka-core api v1' with the left margin and no ANSI on a non-TTY. eka plugin install steward resolves v2.2.0 (checksum-verified) and eka steward version dispatches with the matching margin."}